   "County/Parish/Tribe": "San Juan",
   "Current Status": "6/16/26 - continue to wait on applicant to provide crosscutters reports or info regarding potential work already done by BLM that was requested in October 2025. Applicant has indicated multiple times they are working on it and expected to have it to us already. Applicant is not very responsive and often takes several weeks to respond to inquiries. ESA/NHPA concurrences are essentially the only thing holding up this application from being able to move into the public notice/comment period.\n7/16/26 - applicant remains unresponsive to requests for crosscutters information and/or information regarding coordination with BLM.\n7/24/26 - applicant responded re: follow-up questions team had sent in May, but still no crosscutters reports submitted. Working w/ORC and HQ on next steps, which may include us contracting out the work ourselves, since crosscutters concurrences are the primary items preventing R6 from issuing draft permits and starting the public notice/comment period.\n8/27/26 - followed up again w/applicant re: crosscutters reports and contacts for BLM/DOE.",
