   "Current Status": "RAI 1 deadline extension from March 15th 2024 to April 15th 2024.\n\nRAI 4 deadline extension from February 10th 2025 to March 12 2025.\n\nRAI 6 deadline extension from July 7th, 2025 - August 7th, 2025.\n\nAoR section of application is being delayed due other Class VI projects in the vicinity. The two adjacent Class VI applicants will have their CO2 critical pressure fronts overlap and refuse to speak with Pelican. We are currently working with Pelican to decide on what modeling would be most appropriate given the density of fluids in the reservoir.\n\nRAI sent on Oct 15 2025 with follow up instructions for AoR modeling\n\nPelican Responded to RAI on November 17, however there are still existing errors in their modelling. Pelican subsequently sent a technical note which DOE is currently analyzing and curating guidance for a final direction.\n\nRAI was sent to Pelican Regarding their AoR Modeling\nESA RAI Letter is under review by ORC and will then be routed for signature before sending to PR.\nESA and NHPA RAI's were sent\n\nAwaiting HQ guidance on mixing concentrations and degradation of USDW.\n\nDOE support is no longer available, assessing how long this will delay their permit application timeline. Currently trying to find more modeling support, potential delay could extend beyond 3 months.\n\nSpoke with HQ about the potential for a 1kg threshold for hypothetical leakage into the USDW\n\nRAI 9 is out with the applicant. They had requested a meeting for some clarifications and a letter was sent out subsequently to address their questions.",
